attempts.raw:
@start **The window opens on a long spine.** Columns 0 to 10, `nuoC` to `nuoN`, are carried by 94 to 100% of chromosomes, all persistent, in a region of plasticity in 0% of calls {S1}. The model names 99 to 100% of them, fewest at column 4, `nuoH`, 99% {S1}.

@variable **A fork follows at `yfbM`**, column 11, carried by 89%, with `yfbP` at 27% {S2.c11}. Then columns 13 to 33, `rbn` to `yfaY`, are [[NADH-quinone oxidoreductase]] and menaquinone and arabinose genes, carried by 92 to 94% {S3, Q}. The most plastic stretch is columns 57 to 62, `atoB` to `atoS`, in a region of plasticity in 57 to 76% of calls {S10, P}.

@model **The model names more genes on the spine columns than on the fork and variable ones**, 97 against 93%, and hesitates less there, 0.21 against 0.41 bits {M}. Its most hesitant column, 11, `yfbM`, is a fork column, at 1.21 bits {H}.

@end **The window ends on the `nap` genes.** Columns 73 to 79, `napF` to `napC`, are carried by 36 to 86% of chromosomes, all persistent {S14}. The last column is `napC`, in 36% of chromosomes {E}.

@whole **Across the window it names 96% of genes**, 0.27 bits on average, perplexity 1.3 families {G}. Inside a region of plasticity it hesitates more than outside, 0.59 against 0.21 bits, and names fewer genes, 88% against 97% {C}.

